   "reference": {
    "title": "WHO 5th pleural mesothelioma nuclear grading, BAP1/MTAP & AJCC 9th",
    "intro": "WHO 5th mandates 2-tier nuclear grading (Low vs High grade) for all epithelioid mesotheliomas using nuclear atypia (1–3), mitotic count (1–3), and necrosis. Report % sarcomatoid component in biphasic mesothelioma.",
    "note": "Photomicrographs are from Wikimedia Commons under open Creative Commons licences. ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "Epithelioid 2-tier nuclear grading & ancillary confirmation",
      "points": [
       "Nuclear atypia (1=mild, 2=moderate, 3=severe) + mitotic count (1=<=1/2 mm2, 2=2–4/2 mm2, 3=>=5/2 mm2) = total score 2–6 (Grade I=2–3, Grade II=4–5, Grade III=6). Low grade = Grade I, or Grade II without necrosis; High grade = Grade II with necrosis, or Grade III.",
       "Mesothelial confirmation: at least 2 positive mesothelial markers (calretinin nuclear+cytoplasmic, WT1, D2-40, CK5/6) and 2 negative carcinoma markers (claudin-4, BerEP4, TTF-1, PAX8).",
       "Malignancy vs reactive mesothelial hyperplasia: BAP1 nuclear loss (~50–70% epithelioid) and/or MTAP cytoplasmic loss / CDKN2A (p16) homozygous deletion by FISH."
      ],
      "links": [
       {
        "label": "ExpertPath: Pleural Mesothelioma",
        "url": "https://app.expertpath.com/"
       }
      ],
      "images": [
       {
        "src": "assets/reference/mesothelioma/meso_epithelioid.jpg",
